#====================================================================
# E319 draft — bundled Waf 2.0.x fails after Python removes imp
#====================================================================

id:                     E319
trigger_tool:           waf|python
phase:                  configuration
error_signature:        ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'imp'|AttributeError: module 'imp' has no attribute 'new_module'|waflib/Context\.py.*imp

severity:               2
category:               build-system|python|waf|compatibility
match_keywords:         waf, waflib, Context.py, imp, imp.new_module, ModuleNotFoundError, Python 3.12, ModuleType
title:                  Bundled Waf 2.0.x uses removed Python imp module

root_cause:             Older bundled Waf releases import imp and call imp.new_module(), but Python 3.12 removed the imp module. The build fails before project configuration although the project source and compiler are otherwise valid.
affected_scope:         Projects shipping an unmaintained Waf 2.0.x copy and building it with Python 3.12 or later, including archives rather than a system-upgraded Waf installation.
verification_cmd:       python3 -c "import imp"; python3 -c "from types import ModuleType; print(ModuleType('wscript'))"

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           replace-imp-new-module
rec_description:        Patch only the bundled Waf module loader: replace imp.new_module(name) with types.ModuleType(name), retain the existing exec() and module-cache behavior, and syntax-check the patched module with the target Python.
rec_command:            sed -i 's/import os, re, imp, sys/import os, re, sys\\nfrom types import ModuleType/; s/imp.new_module(WSCRIPT_FILE)/ModuleType(WSCRIPT_FILE)/' waflib/Context.py && python3 -m py_compile waflib/Context.py
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      use-supported-python
fallback_description:   Run the unpatched bundled Waf with Python 3.11 or earlier only when the project policy permits a pinned host Python and the package does not need Python 3.12 compatibility.
fallback_command:       python3.11 ./waf configure
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          set-env-var

forbid_1_pattern:       pip install waf|replace.*bundled.*waf.*without.*review
forbid_1_reason:        Replacing a vendored Waf release changes build behavior beyond the incompatible module-loader call and can make a package non-reproducible.
forbid_1_consequence:   Configuration semantics, generated files, or install tasks can change independently of the compatibility repair.
forbid_2_pattern:       ignore.*ModuleNotFoundError.*imp|skip.*waf.*configure
forbid_2_reason:        The error is deterministic and occurs before configuration; skipping it produces no valid build evidence.
forbid_2_consequence:   A PR can falsely claim a package was configured or built.

principles:             P002, P003
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E055, E177]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/E319-draft-ASP1-waf-python312.md
last_updated:           2026-08-12
source_event:           JACK 1.9.22 PR #3482 bundled Waf 2.0.12
authors:                ASP1R1N <sukurajimayilei@gmail.com>
source_pr:              3482
source_commit:          3dd7cf1ba
metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     1.0
metrics_last_used:      2026-08-12
draft:                  true
contributor_id:         ASP1
